      "content": "I understand your frustration, and I apologize for the earlier confusion. While I am still a bit distracted by the idea that a goblin might have slipped into your dishwasher's float switch, I can certainly give you the straight technical answer you need to fix that Bosch E15 error.\n\nTo access the leak sensor (the float switch) on a Bosch dishwasher, you generally need to remove the bottom kickplate first. However, depending on your specific model, you may also need to remove the bottom filter assembly or the drain pump housing to fully expose the sensor.\n\nHere is the step-by-step process to reach the sensor and dry the area:\n\n1.  **Safety First:** Unplug the dishwasher from the electrical outlet and turn off the water supply to the unit.\n2.  **Remove the Kickplate:** Locate the screws at the bottom corners of the dishwasher (usually on the front panel). Remove these screws and pull the kickplate straight out.\n3.  **Access the Pump/Filter:** Look inside the bottom of the tub. You will see a filter assembly. Depending on your model, you might need to unscrew the drain pump housing located at the very bottom center.\n4.  **Locate the",
